WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.363
need to discuss our plan while we eat because there is not much time," said Sherlock Holmes as

2
00:00:20.423 --> 00:00:21.844
Mrs. Hudson brought in our supper.

3
00:00:21.864 --> 00:00:26.787
"It is nearly five o'clock now, and in two hours we must be at Briony Lodge when Irene

4
00:00:26.887 --> 00:00:30.910
Adler—or rather Irene Norton—returns from her drive at seven o'clock."

5
00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.531
"And what then?"

6
00:00:32.952 --> 00:00:33.372
I asked.

7
00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:35.273
"You must leave that to me.

8
00:00:36.213 --> 00:00:39.355
I have already arranged what will occur, but I insist on one thing.

9
00:00:40.356 --> 00:00:42.418
You must not interfere no matter what happens.

10
00:00:43.338 --> 00:00:44.419
Do you understand, Watson?"

11
00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:46.760
"I'm to do nothing," I said.

12
00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.381
"That is correct.

13
00:00:49.322 --> 00:00:51.183
There will probably be a little disturbance.

14
00:00:52.164 --> 00:00:53.025
Do not join in.

15
00:00:54.005 --> 00:00:56.487
The disturbance will end with my being carried into the house.

16
00:00:57.648 --> 00:01:00.510
Four or five minutes later someone will open the sitting-room window.

17
00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:03.912
You are to position yourself close to that open window."

18
00:01:04.928 --> 00:01:05.308
"All right."

19
00:01:05.328 --> 00:01:09.170
"I will be visible to you, so keep your eye on me.

20
00:01:10.151 --> 00:01:14.713
When I raise my hand like this, you will throw something into the room and shout, 'Fire!'"

21
00:01:15.694 --> 00:01:16.334
I was puzzled.

22
00:01:16.354 --> 00:01:18.195
"But what am I to throw?"

23
00:01:18.215 --> 00:01:23.478
"This smoke bomb," said Holmes, taking a long, cigar-shaped object from his pocket.

24
00:01:23.498 --> 00:01:29.642
"It's nothing very sophisticated, just a simple device that plumbers use to detect where pipes are leaking.

25
00:01:30.562 --> 00:01:33.484
When you shout, 'Fire,' quite a number of people will join in.

26
00:01:34.476 --> 00:01:37.737
You should then walk to the end of the street, where I will meet you in ten minutes.

27
00:01:38.737 --> 00:01:39.838
Have I made myself clear?"

28
00:01:40.818 --> 00:01:42.239
"Quite so," I replied.

29
00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:44.519
"You may rely entirely on me."

30
00:01:44.539 --> 00:01:50.041
"Excellent! And now it is soon time for me to prepare for the new role I have to

31
00:01:50.081 --> 00:01:54.223
play." After finishing his supper, Holmes disappeared into his bedroom.

32
00:01:55.203 --> 00:01:58.204
When he emerged, he was disguised as an amiable clergyman.

33
00:01:59.808 --> 00:02:06.391
His broad black hat and baggy trousers, his sympathetic smile and general look of benevolent curiosity all contributed

34
00:02:06.471 --> 00:02:07.411
to his new character.

35
00:02:08.312 --> 00:02:10.613
It was not merely that Holmes had changed his clothes.

36
00:02:11.073 --> 00:02:16.655
His expression, his manner, his very soul seemed to vary with every fresh part that he assumed.

37
00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:20.617
The stage had lost a fine actor when he became a detective.

38
00:02:21.557 --> 00:02:25.999
It was quarter past six when we left Baker Street, but it was still ten minutes before seven

39
00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:27.380
when we arrived at our destination.

40
00:02:28.392 --> 00:02:31.194
In front of Briony Lodge, the streetlamps were just being lighted.

41
00:02:32.095 --> 00:02:36.838
The house looked exactly as I'd pictured it from Holmes' description, but I was surprised at how busy

42
00:02:36.878 --> 00:02:37.519
the street was.

43
00:02:38.499 --> 00:02:43.283
There were a group of shabbily dressed men smoking and loafing at the corner, a scissors grinder working

44
00:02:43.303 --> 00:02:48.987
at his wheel, two soldiers flirting with a nurse, and several well-dressed young men and women walking back

45
00:02:49.027 --> 00:02:49.447
and forth.

46
00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:53.450
"Now where are we to find this photograph?"

47
00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.332
said Holmes as we paced up and down in front of the house.

48
00:02:57.328 --> 00:02:59.289
"Irene probably does not carry it with her.

49
00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:04.092
She knows that the king is capable of having her stopped and searched because he has done that

50
00:03:04.152 --> 00:03:04.832
twice already."

51
00:03:04.852 --> 00:03:07.014
"Then where is the photograph?"

52
00:03:07.414 --> 00:03:07.834
I asked.

53
00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:11.957
"Possibly with her lawyer or banker, but I'm inclined to think not.

54
00:03:12.957 --> 00:03:14.698
Why should she hand it over to anyone else?

55
00:03:15.699 --> 00:03:18.100
Remember that she has resolved to use it in a few days.

56
00:03:19.141 --> 00:03:21.582
It must be where she can easily lay her hands on it.

57
00:03:22.563 --> 00:03:24.484
The photograph must be in her own house."

58
00:03:25.528 --> 00:03:28.310
"But her house has been broken into twice," I protested.

59
00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.911
"The burglars didn't know how to look for it."

60
00:03:30.931 --> 00:03:32.732
"But how will you look?"

61
00:03:32.752 --> 00:03:35.894
"I will not look," Holmes said mysteriously.

62
00:03:35.914 --> 00:03:38.776
"I will get her to show me where she has hidden it."

63
00:03:38.796 --> 00:03:43.159
"Oh, she will refuse to do that," I told him.

64
00:03:43.179 --> 00:03:45.400
"She will not be able to refuse.

65
00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:46.701
But hark!

66
00:03:47.581 --> 00:03:49.042
I hear the rumble of carriage wheels.

67
00:03:49.983 --> 00:03:51.924
Now carry out my orders exactly as I said."

68
00:03:52.944 --> 00:03:55.806
As he spoke, a carriage rattled up to the door of Briony Lodge.

69
00:03:56.806 --> 00:04:01.129
When it arrived, one of the shabbily dressed men at the corner dashed forward to open the door.

70
00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:06.172
He obviously hoped that the lovely female passenger would reward him with a few coins.

71
00:04:07.172 --> 00:04:10.855
But he was elbowed aside by another loafer, who had rushed up with the same intention.

72
00:04:11.895 --> 00:04:16.398
A fierce quarrel broke out as the two soldiers sided with the first man while the scissors grinder

73
00:04:16.558 --> 00:04:18.019
argued on behalf of the second man.

74
00:04:19.059 --> 00:04:19.820
A blow was struck.

75
00:04:20.872 --> 00:04:24.755
In an instant the lady, who had stepped from her carriage, was in the center of a circle

76
00:04:24.815 --> 00:04:29.398
of flushed and struggling men, who struck savagely at each other with fists and sticks.

77
00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:35.262
Holmes dashed into the crowd to protect the lady, but just as he reached her, he gave a

78
00:04:35.322 --> 00:04:36.603
cry and dropped to the ground.

79
00:04:37.503 --> 00:04:39.265
Blood was running freely down his face.

80
00:04:40.365 --> 00:04:43.848
As he fell, the soldiers took off in one direction and the loafers in the other.

81
00:04:44.932 --> 00:04:49.316
Some of the well-dressed people, who had watched the scuffle but not joined in, crowded in to help

82
00:04:49.356 --> 00:04:51.438
the lady and attend to the injured clergyman.

83
00:04:52.498 --> 00:04:56.902
Irene Adler, as I will continue to call her, hurried up the steps, but she paused at the

84
00:04:56.922 --> 00:04:58.523
door and looked back into the street.

85
00:04:58.543 --> 00:05:01.065
"Is the poor clergyman badly hurt?"

86
00:05:01.426 --> 00:05:01.926
she asked.

87
00:05:02.927 --> 00:05:03.547
"He is dead!"

88
00:05:03.888 --> 00:05:04.808
cried several voices.

89
00:05:04.828 --> 00:05:07.210
"No, no, there's life in him!"

90
00:05:07.591 --> 00:05:08.231
shouted another.

91
00:05:08.251 --> 00:05:11.154
"But he'll be gone before you can get him to a hospital."

92
00:05:11.174 --> 00:05:13.776
"He's a brave fellow," said a woman.

93
00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.342
"They would have stolen the lady's purse and watch if it hadn't been for him.

94
00:05:17.362 --> 00:05:20.585
"They were a gang and a rough one too!

95
00:05:21.686 --> 00:05:22.786
Ah, he's breathing now."

96
00:05:22.806 --> 00:05:25.749
"He can't lie in the street," said a man.

97
00:05:25.769 --> 00:05:28.031
"May we bring him inside, ma'am?"

98
00:05:28.971 --> 00:05:30.673
"Of course," said Irene Adler.

99
00:05:30.693 --> 00:05:34.155
"Bring him into the sitting room where there is a comfortable sofa.

100
00:05:35.136 --> 00:05:35.997
Come this way, please."

101
00:05:37.038 --> 00:05:39.860
Slowly and solemnly Holmes was carried into Briony Lodge.

102
00:05:40.864 --> 00:05:44.407
The lamps had been lit, but the blinds had not been drawn in the sitting room, so I

103
00:05:44.447 --> 00:05:45.928
could see Holmes lying on the couch.

104
00:05:46.988 --> 00:05:50.851
I don't know if he felt any remorse, but I felt heartily ashamed of myself when I saw

105
00:05:50.891 --> 00:05:52.712
that beautiful creature kindly tending to him.

106
00:05:53.733 --> 00:05:56.515
And yet it would have been the worst treachery to abandon Holmes now.

107
00:05:57.596 --> 00:06:00.277
I hardened my heart and took the smoke bomb from under my coat.

108
00:06:01.338 --> 00:06:05.281
After all, we were not injuring her; we were keeping her from injuring another person.

109
00:06:07.002 --> 00:06:09.684
Suddenly Holmes sat up and motioned like a man in need of air.

110
00:06:10.748 --> 00:06:12.449
A maid rushed to the window and opened it.

111
00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:17.532
At the same moment he raised his hand, and I tossed my smoke bomb into the room and

112
00:06:17.592 --> 00:06:18.673
cried, "Fire!"

113
00:06:19.713 --> 00:06:22.895
Instantly the whole crowd of spectators joined and cried, "Fire!"

114
00:06:23.895 --> 00:06:26.517
Thick clouds of smoke curled through the room and out the window.

115
00:06:27.477 --> 00:06:32.160
I caught a glimpse of rushing figures, and a moment later I heard Holmes reassuring everyone inside that

116
00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.181
it was a false alarm.

117
00:06:34.141 --> 00:06:38.484
Slipping through the shouting crowd outside, I made my way down the street, where I was soon joined

118
00:06:38.504 --> 00:06:39.004
by Holmes.

119
00:06:40.044 --> 00:06:42.625
"You did that very nicely, Watson," said Holmes.

120
00:06:42.645 --> 00:06:44.786
"Everything is all right now."

121
00:06:45.726 --> 00:06:46.687
"You have the photograph?"

122
00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:47.507
I asked.

123
00:06:48.548 --> 00:06:51.149
"No," he answered, "but I know where it is."
